# summarize.py's resume sidecar. It lives inside the committed threads dir but
# is not thread data, and it only survives a date that finished with failures —
# exactly when `git add data/threads/` runs. Committed once, it is permanent
# until that same date next completes cleanly, and every consumer that reads the
# directory would have to keep filtering it (#52).
# Resume is unaffected: summarize.py rebuilds `completed` from the threads file
# when the sidecar is absent. One cost — a meeting that completed but produced
# no thread leaves no trace to rebuild from, so it is re-grouped on later runs
# within the lookback window. Wasted grouping calls, never duplicate threads.
data/threads/*.progress.json

# write_json_atomic's in-flight temp file (scripts/pipeline/jsonio.py, and the
# same shape in scripts/validate-data.mjs). It cleans up after itself on any
# exception, but a SIGKILL — the workflow's 120-minute timeout, the OOM killer —
# runs no cleanup at all, and `git add data/threads/` would then commit the
# stray file permanently. No slash, so it matches at any depth.
.*.tmp

# Pipeline output (committed for SSG deployment)
# data/threads/   — thread JSON files
# data/members.json — member data
# data/status.json — processing status

# Article drafts (not published)
drafts/

# Handoff / prototype (not part of source)
HANDOFF.md
kokkai-v5.jsx

# apps/mcp/data/ is a build-time copy of repo-root data/ (see apps/mcp/scripts/copy-data.mjs).
